{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.QIntegerCanonical"],"declarations":25,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":366,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L366-L377","doc":"**H_3 case for `(1,1,1)`**: `y_{(1,1,1)}(q) = (q⁻¹)^3 / ((q + q⁻¹)(q^2 + 1 + q⁻²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_mid","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_mid","kind":"theorem","line":354,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L354-L364","doc":"**H_3 case for `(2,1)`**: `y_{(2,1)}(q) = 1 / ((q + q⁻¹)(q^2 + 1 + q⁻²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H3_top","kind":"theorem","line":341,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L341-L352","doc":"**H_3 case for `(3)`**: `y_(3)(q) = q^3 / ((q + q⁻¹)(q^2 + 1 + q⁻²))`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_sq_add_one_add_inv_sq_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_sq_add_one_add_inv_sq_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":337,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L337-L339","doc":"Non-vanishing of `q² + 1 + (q⁻¹)²`, via strict positivity. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_sq_add_one_add_inv_sq_pos","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_sq_add_one_add_inv_sq_pos","kind":"theorem","line":330,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L330-L335","doc":"Strict positivity of `q² + 1 + (q⁻¹)²` for any real `q` (sum of\ntwo squares plus 1).  Helper shared across the H_3 identities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_add_inv_ne_zero","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.q_add_inv_ne_zero","kind":"theorem","line":321,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L321-L328","doc":"Non-vanishing of `q + q⁻¹` for any real `q ≠ 0` (since `q² = -1`\nhas no real solution).  Helper shared across the H_3 identities. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_normalization","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_normalization","kind":"theorem","line":284,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L284-L300","doc":"**H_2 Plancherel normalization**: `y_(2)(q) + y_{(1,1)}(q) = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_bottom","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_bottom","kind":"theorem","line":275,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L275-L282","doc":"**H_2 case for `(1,1)`**: `y_{(1,1)}(q) = q⁻¹ / (q + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_top","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qSchur_H2_top","kind":"theorem","line":267,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L267-L273","doc":"**H_2 case for `(2)`**: `y_(2)(q) = q / (q + q⁻¹)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial_three","kind":"theorem","line":253,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L253-L257","doc":"**`[3]_q! = (q² + 1 + q⁻²)(q + q⁻¹)`** (`= [3]_q · [2]_q!`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial_two","kind":"theorem","line":246,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L246-L251","doc":"**`[2]_q! = q + q⁻¹`** (`= [2]_q · [1]_q`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_three","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_three","kind":"theorem","line":237,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L237-L244","doc":"**`[3]_q = q² + 1 + q⁻²`** — difference of cubes over `q − q⁻¹`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_two","kind":"theorem","line":228,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L228-L235","doc":"**`[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`**. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_one","kind":"theorem","line":221,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L221-L226","doc":"**`[1]_q = 1`** (for valid `q`, i.e. `q − q⁻¹ ≠ 0`). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.closed_form_holds","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.closed_form_holds","kind":"theorem","line":211,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L211-L211","doc":"**The conjecture**: the closed form `ySchurClosedForm` agrees\nwith the q-Schur weight `qSchurWeight` at every partition and\nevery valid q, i.e. `y_λ^{qSchur}(q) = q^{c(λ)} / [n]_q!`. Any\ninstance of this class commits to that extensional identification.\n\n**Provenance corrected 2026-08-24 (bean `qou-2joi`).** This read\n\"the Lusztig 1990 / BLM identity\" and carried a single\n`-- Ref: [lusztig1990]`. That key is *Canonical bases arising from\nquantized enveloping algebras* (JAMS 3), which is not where a\nq-Schur Markov-trace weight identity lives; the q-Schur source is\nBLM, now `[blm1990]`. Two further cautions before anyone treats\nthis as settled-in-the-literature rather than open here:\n\n* `blm1990` is **UNVERIFIED** — added from recall because the\n  bibliography had zero q-Schur entries, and neither paper is in\n  `library/`, so nothing in this repo can check the identity as\n  stated. `lusztig1990` has no entry in\n  `folio/bib-qa-verifications.json` either.\n* The corpus asserts **two different DOIs** for `lusztig1990`:\n  `10.2307/1990961` in `folio/schema/references.ts`, and\n  `10.2307/2152736` in `QOU/OptionE/CrystalDeltaLambdaScaffold.lean`\n  and `QOU/IwahoriHecke/TypeA.lean`. Not resolved here — guessing\n  which is right is exactly what produced the discrepancy. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.qSchurWeight","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.qSchurWeight","kind":"def","line":187,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L187-L187","doc":"The categorical q-Schur Markov-trace Plancherel weight,\nawaiting Mathlib's q-Schur algebra formalisation. Until then\nthis field is provided abstractly by any instance of the\nclass; the conjecture is `closed_form_holds` below. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim.mk","kind":"ctor","line":182,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L182-L182","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.QSchurYLambdaClosedFormClaim","kind":"class","line":160,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L160-L211","doc":"**Conjecture (axiomatised as class per AGENTS.md §3b-cond)**.\n\nFor every partition `λ` and every valid `q : ℝ`, the q-Schur\nMarkov-trace Plancherel weight `y_λ^{qSchur}(q)` equals the\nclosed form `ySchurClosedForm λ q = q^{c(λ)} / [n]_q!`.\n\nThis is a known theorem in q-Schur duality (Lusztig 1990,\nBeilinson–Lusztig–MacPherson) but its Lean formalisation from\nMathlib axioms requires the q-Schur algebra structure not\ncurrently in Mathlib. The class axiomatises this via an abstract\n`qSchurWeight` field (the categorical weight, awaiting the\nMathlib formalisation) and an extensional `closed_form_holds`\nidentity asserting equality with `ySchurClosedForm` everywhere.\nDownstream theorems depending on this closed form take this\nclass as an `[Instance]` hypothesis per §3b-cond.\n\nConvention deviation note: most §3b-cond classes in the\nrepository (~80-100, registered under\n`lean-section-3b-cond-classes-permanent`) use a vacuous\n`True` placeholder field. This class uses the stronger\nextensional form per PR #1720 review (Gemini, 2026-06-03);\nthe repo-wide convention is unchanged. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.ySchurClosedForm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.ySchurClosedForm","kind":"def","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L155-L158","doc":"q-Schur Plancherel weight closed form: `y_λ(q) = q^{c(λ)} / [n]_q!`\nwhere `n = |λ|` is the partition size. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qFactorial","kind":"def","line":150,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L150-L153","doc":"q-factorial `[n]_q! = Π_{k=1}^{n} [k]_q`. At `n = 0` returns 1. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_eq_canonical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket_eq_canonical","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L135-L148","doc":"**Bridge to the canonical balanced bracket, and the guard is redundant.**\n\nThis site guards the singular locus `q − q⁻¹ = 0` and returns `0` there — which\nis exactly what the *unguarded* `qIntBal` already returns, since Lean's\n`x / 0 = 0`.  So unlike the sites that guard to `n`, this one is not a\nclassical extension at all: it agrees with the plain canonical bracket\neverywhere, and needs no hypothesis. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.qBracket","kind":"def","line":123,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L123-L133","doc":"q-integer `[k]_q = (q^k − q^{-k}) / (q − q^{-1})` for `k : ℕ`.\n\nReturns `0` if `q − q⁻¹ = 0` (i.e. `q = ±1`, the degenerate case\nwhere the bracket is not well-defined). For valid `q`:\n- `[0]_q = 0`\n- `[1]_q = 1`\n- `[2]_q = q + q⁻¹`\n- `[n]_q = q^{n-1} + q^{n-3} + ... + q^{-(n-1)}` (n terms) ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.contentSum.go","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.contentSum.go","kind":"def","line":119,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L119-L121","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.contentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.contentSum","kind":"def","line":111,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L111-L121","doc":"Content sum `c(λ) = Σ_{(i,j) ∈ λ} (j − i)` for a partition `λ`\nrepresented as a list of row lengths.\n\nRow index `i` (0-based) and column index `j` (0-based); each cell\n`(i, j)` contributes `j - i` to the sum. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.rowContentSum","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.BraidsAndKnots.QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.rowContentSum","kind":"def","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/BraidsAndKnots/QSchurYLambdaClosedForm.lean#L101-L109","doc":"Row contribution to content sum for a row of length `row` starting at\nrow-index `i`: `Σ_{j=0}^{row-1} (j - i)`.\n\nDefined by structural recursion on `row` (rather than `Finset.range`)\nso that closed evaluations `rowContentSum r i` reduce in the kernel —\nused by the `decide` proofs of the H_2 / H_3 content sums below. ","signatureChunk":0}]}